ID: Ch3-Second-Feeling
TEXT:

As the adrenaline ebbs, the reality sinks in: this was the first time I have taken human lives. It was...

choice("Easy", Ch3-Second-Easy, v_current_scene = Ch3-Second-Easy)
choice("Necessary", Ch3-Second-Necessary, v_current_scene = Ch3-Second-Necessary)
choice("Horrifying", Ch3-Second-Horrifying, v_current_scene = Ch3-Second-Horrifying)


ID: Ch3-Second-Easy
TEXT:

...easy. Easier than I imagined. My pulse stays steady, my hands calm. In a survival contest against a hundred armed mercenaries, hesitation is suicide. It is a relief to know my resolve won't buckle under blood.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Glance, v_current_scene = Ch3-Glance) if (v_ch3_saved_from_dart == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Decide-Killed, v_current_scene = Ch3-Decide-Killed) if (v_ch3_saved_from_dart == 0)


ID: Ch3-Second-Necessary
TEXT:

...necessary. No joy in it, but they chose to hunt mages in these woods. They came armed with poison and repeaters, fully intending to execute us where we stood. In combat, you kill or you die.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Glance, v_current_scene = Ch3-Glance) if (v_ch3_saved_from_dart == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Decide-Killed, v_current_scene = Ch3-Decide-Killed) if (v_ch3_saved_from_dart == 0)


ID: Ch3-Second-Horrifying
TEXT:

...horrifying. Blood pools in the moss around the five corpses, steaming in the cold mountain air. Five lives wiped out in seconds. I force the sickness down and grip my crossbow tighter—Kate is in danger, and I cannot allow remorse to freeze my limbs.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Glance, v_current_scene = Ch3-Glance) if (v_ch3_saved_from_dart == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Decide-Killed, v_current_scene = Ch3-Decide-Killed) if (v_ch3_saved_from_dart == 0)


ID: Ch3-Glance
TEXT:

I peer back toward the clearing through the trees.

Kate has already shattered the stalemate. Above the smoke line, massive frost fans roar as they scatter the chemical fog into thin air. In the moonlight above her head, hundreds of razor-sharp ice blades form in a lethal canopy. With a single gesture, she rains them down upon the mercenaries, wiping out the entire front line in a blizzard of blood and iron.

She didn't need my assistance after all. With the perimeter cleared, I jog back into the clearing.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Ice-hand, v_current_scene = Ch3-Ice-hand)


ID: Ch3-Give
TEXT:

"Give me an ice dagger," I say.

Kate blinks through the pain, staring at me as if I've lost my senses. "What?"

"You heard me. Forge a dagger. I'm going out there."

"You are insane. What do you plan to do, talk a hundred mercenaries to death?"

"Give me the blade, or I go out barehanded. Your choice."

Recognizing the stubbornness in my jaw, Kate grinds her teeth and weaves frost between her palms, handing me a twelve-inch stiletto of dense blue ice. The grip bites into my skin with freezing cold, but the balance is lethal.

"Keep the dome sealed while I work," I tell her. "Stay on pure defense. Don't take unnecessary risks."

"Are you certain of this?"

"Completely. Open a seam."

She parts an exit just wide enough for me to slip through. I dive into the smoking woods, boots digging into the pine needles.

Thirty yards in, I spot a mercenary crouching behind a wide oak trunk, his back turned as he cranks the lever on his repeating crossbow. He hasn't heard a sound.

choice("Kill him with my dagger", Ch3-First-kill, v_current_scene = Ch3-First-kill, v_ch3_first_killed = 1)
choice("Use the hilt of the dagger to knock him out", Ch3-First-Knock, v_current_scene = Ch3-First-Knock)


ID: Ch3-Decide-Killed
TEXT:

I strip the extra bolt quivers from the first man's belt, slinging them over my shoulder before pushing deeper into the dark timber.

Before I engage the main force, I need to decide my rule of engagement for the rest of the company.

choice("Don't kill any of them, only incapacitate them", Ch3-Incapacitate, v_current_scene = Ch3-Incapacitate, v_ch3_prioritize = 1)
choice("Only kill when there's no other viable alternative", Ch3-Viable, v_current_scene = Ch3-Viable, v_ch3_prioritize = 2)
choice("Prioritize killing, but don't chase after them if they run away", Ch3-Prioritize, v_current_scene = Ch3-Prioritize, v_ch3_prioritize = 3)
choice("Kill every single one of the crossbowmen, and leave no survivors", Ch3-Every, v_current_scene = Ch3-Every, v_ch3_prioritize = 4)


ID: Ch3-Decide-Alive
TEXT:

Before moving out, I strip the extra bolt quivers from the unconscious man's harness, slinging them over my shoulder.

Before I engage the main force, I need to decide my rule of engagement for the rest of the company.

choice("Don't kill any of them, only incapacitate them", Ch3-Incapacitate, v_current_scene = Ch3-Incapacitate, v_ch3_prioritize = 1)
choice("Only kill when there's no other viable alternative", Ch3-Viable, v_current_scene = Ch3-Viable, v_ch3_prioritize = 2)
choice("Prioritize killing, but don't chase after them if they run away", Ch3-Prioritize, v_current_scene = Ch3-Prioritize, v_ch3_prioritize = 3)
choice("Kill every single one of the crossbowmen, and leave no survivors", Ch3-Every, v_current_scene = Ch3-Every, v_ch3_prioritize = 4)


ID: Ch3-Incapacitate
TEXT:

set(v_ch3_tried_lift,0) if (v_strength == 0)
set(v_ch3_tried_lift,1) if (v_strength >= 1)
#if(v_strength == 0) {

Just because they ambushed us with poison doesn't mean I have to butcher them. Many are hirelings following orders for copper, with families waiting across the sea. I will aim to disable—shattered limbs and disarmed hands, but no corpses.

The tactical problem remains: Kate's ice dome is under continuous barrage, frost cracking under dozens of impacts every second. She has no window to retaliate.

The mercenaries are positioned in interlocking fire teams behind heavy timber. To break them non-lethally, I either need overwhelming speed to disarm them in close quarters, or the skill to fire accurately on the run.

Sniping from extreme range is an option, but picking off limbs through dense night foliage at distance will burn precious minutes Kate doesn't have.

}
#if(v_strength >= 1) {

Just because they ambushed us with poison doesn't mean I have to butcher them. Many are hirelings following orders for copper, with families waiting across the sea. I will aim to disable—shattered limbs and disarmed hands, but no corpses.

The tactical problem remains: Kate's ice dome is under continuous barrage, frost cracking under dozens of impacts every second. She has no window to retaliate.

The mercenaries are positioned in interlocking fire teams behind heavy timber. To break them non-lethally, I either need overwhelming speed to disarm them in close quarters, or the skill to fire accurately on the run.

Sniping from extreme range is an option, but picking off limbs through dense night foliage at distance will burn precious minutes Kate doesn't have.

My gaze falls upon a massive fallen pine trunk beside me, its bark stripped and thick as a beer barrel. I set my boots into the needles and grip the wood.

}
choice("Continue", Ch3-Lift, v_current_scene = Ch3-Lift)


ID: Ch3-Viable
TEXT:

set(v_ch3_tried_lift,0) if (v_strength == 0)
set(v_ch3_tried_lift,1) if (v_strength >= 1)
#if(v_strength == 0) {

I didn't enter this tournament to become a butcher. But I won't risk my throat to protect men who came to slit ours. If an enemy can be disarmed, I spare him; if he forces the issue, I put an iron bolt through his chest.

The tactical problem remains: Kate's ice dome is under continuous barrage, frost cracking under dozens of impacts every second. She has no window to retaliate.

The mercenaries are positioned in interlocking fire teams behind heavy timber. To neutralize them quickly, I need either raw speed to flank their cover, or the technique to shoot on the move.

Sniping from extreme range is an option, but picking off targets through dense night foliage at distance will burn precious minutes Kate doesn't have.

}
