These men ambushed us with poison darts and vowed to slit our throats. They offered no mercy, and they deserve none. I won't waste time chasing broken deserters into the dark, but anyone holding a weapon dies.

The tactical problem remains: Kate's ice dome is under continuous barrage, frost cracking under dozens of impacts every second. She has no window to retaliate.

The mercenaries are positioned in interlocking fire teams behind heavy timber. To wipe them out before Kate's mana breaks, I need either raw speed to storm their positions, or the technique to shoot on the move.

Sniping from extreme range is an option, but methodical shooting through dense night foliage at distance will burn precious minutes Kate doesn't have.

My gaze falls upon a massive fallen pine trunk beside me, its bark stripped and thick as a beer barrel. I set my boots into the needles and grip the wood.

