I retrace my steps to the first skirmish site, repeating crossbow cocked. The man I knocked unconscious lies sprawled in the needles. I step over him, line up the iron sights with his temple, and pull the trigger. A muffled crack, and he goes limp forever.

I turn back toward the battle line.

The tactical problem remains: Kate's ice dome is under continuous barrage, frost cracking under dozens of impacts every second. She has no window to retaliate.

