ID: Ch3-Lift
TEXT:

set(v_ch3_lift_tree,1) if (v_ch3_tried_lift == 1 && v_strength == 3)
set(v_ch3_lift_tree,0) if (v_ch3_tried_lift == 1 && v_strength < 3 || v_ch3_tried_lift == 0)
#if(v_ch3_tried_lift == 1 && v_strength == 3 && v_ch3_prioritize >= 3) {

I heave with both arms. The massive four-hundred-pound pine trunk tears free from the earth with a groan of roots and soil, resting easily against my shoulder. The stat booster has pushed my muscular density into the realm of myth.

With timber like this in hand, precision and stealth become secondary. I can wield fallen trunks as battering rams or launch them through the trees like siege engines.

Time is bleeding away. I need to pick my angle of attack and execute.

}
#if(v_ch3_tried_lift == 1 && v_strength == 3 && v_ch3_prioritize < 3) {

I heave with both arms. The massive four-hundred-pound pine trunk tears free from the earth with a groan of roots and soil, resting easily against my shoulder. The stat booster has pushed my muscular density into the realm of myth.

With timber like this in hand, precision and stealth become secondary. I can wield fallen trunks as battering rams or launch them through the trees like siege engines.

Hurl a four-hundred-pound tree into a crowd, however, and bones shatter like dry twigs. If I commit to this weapon, casualties are unavoidable.

Time is bleeding away. I need to pick my angle of attack and execute.

}
#if(v_ch3_tried_lift == 1 && v_strength < 3) {

I haul against the bark with everything I have. The timber barely shivers in the dirt. At least four hundred pounds of solid pine—my physical enhancement isn't high enough to lift siege lumber.

Time is bleeding away. I need to pick a realistic tactic and move.

}
#if(v_ch3_tried_lift == 0) {
Time is bleeding away. I need to pick my strategy and move.

}
choice("Rely on speed and use melee attacks", Ch3-Final-decision, v_current_scene = Ch3-Final-decision, v_ch3_tactic = 1) if (v_ch3_tried_lift == 0 || v_strength == 3 || v_strength < 3)
choice("Try to aim the crossbow while moving", Ch3-Final-decision, v_current_scene = Ch3-Final-decision, v_ch3_tactic = 2) if (v_ch3_tried_lift == 0 || v_strength == 3 || v_strength < 3)
choice("Snipe them from a distance", Ch3-Final-decision, v_current_scene = Ch3-Final-decision, v_ch3_tactic = 3) if (v_ch3_tried_lift == 0 || v_strength == 3 || v_strength < 3)
choice("Use fallen trees for throwing and clobbering", Ch3-Final-decision, v_current_scene = Ch3-Final-decision, v_ch3_tactic = 4) if (v_ch3_tried_lift == 1 && v_strength == 3)


ID: Ch3-Final-decision
TEXT:

The last choice is target priority: strike directly at the commander, or systematically break his firing lines. Capturing their leader might force an immediate surrender and spare Kate's mana; failing to seize him leaves me exposed in the center of their command guard.

choice("Go for the leader, and try to avoid troops on the way", Ch3-Leader, v_current_scene = Ch3-Leader, v_ch3_final_decision = 1)
choice("Go for the crossbowmen first", Ch3-Troops, v_current_scene = Ch3-Troops, v_ch3_final_decision = 2)


ID: Ch3-Leader
TEXT:

Speed is life. Taking down a hundred mercenaries individually will take too long, and Kate's ice dome is already fracturing under the storm of iron. I break toward the rear where the shrill commands originated.

I circle deep through the timber to keep off their firing lanes, tracking the sound of the war horn. Secure in his overwhelming numbers, their commander has likely remained stationary.

As I cut through a grove of birch, dry branches snap ahead. Ten mercenaries in leather brigandines step through the trees, crossbows leveling as they spot my silhouette.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Speed, v_current_scene = Ch3-Speed) if (v_ch3_tactic == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Snipe-first, v_current_scene = Ch3-Snipe-first) if (v_ch3_tactic == 3)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Move-first, v_current_scene = Ch3-Move-first) if (v_ch3_tactic == 2)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Clobber, v_current_scene = Ch3-Clobber) if (v_ch3_tactic == 4)


ID: Ch3-Troops
TEXT:

I cannot throw away the element of surprise on a reckless gamble. The company's focus is entirely locked on Kate's glowing frost dome. By the time their commander realizes his perimeter is collapsing, his battalion will be in pieces.

I circle wide through the dark timber, keeping clear of the command post's line of sight.

As I flank around a cluster of white birch, dry branches snap ahead. Ten mercenaries in leather brigandines step through the trees, crossbows leveling as they spot my silhouette.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Speed, v_current_scene = Ch3-Speed) if (v_ch3_tactic == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Snipe-first, v_current_scene = Ch3-Snipe-first) if (v_ch3_tactic == 3)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Move-first, v_current_scene = Ch3-Move-first) if (v_ch3_tactic == 2)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Clobber, v_current_scene = Ch3-Clobber) if (v_ch3_tactic == 4)


ID: Ch3-Speed
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_agility < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_agility == 3)
#if(v_agility < 3) {

I break cover and charge across the open brush, hoping speed will close the gap.

I am nowhere near fast enough. Stepping into the open without maximum enhancement makes me an easy target. Ten crossbows fire in unison—a wall of iron bolts tears through my chest and throat before I cover half the distance.

}
#if(v_agility == 3) {

I break cover in a blur of movement, surging across the brush.

Three bolts hiss through the air where my chest was a fraction of a second ago. Closing with a melee weapon against ten loaded crossbows is madness, but raw speed is my only edge. If I stop for a single breath, a bolt takes my skull. I have to break their formation.

I sprint wide through the timber, using superior velocity to vanish into the deep pines. Once they lose visual contact, I fire three bolts into distant tree trunks across the ravine. The sharp thwacks echo through the dark.

Four mercenaries take the bait, breaking formation to investigate the noise.

Untrained hirelings. Seasoned soldiers would never scatter their line for an unconfirmed sound in the dark.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_agility < 3)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_agility < 3)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_agility < 3)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Speed2, v_current_scene = Ch3-Speed2) if (v_agility == 3)


ID: Ch3-Snipe-first
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_ch3_lift_tree == 0 && v_perception < 3 || v_ch3_lift_tree == 1 && v_perception < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_perception == 3)
#if(v_perception < 3) {

I raise the repeating crossbow, trying to pick off the patrol from range.

In the pitch-black woods, shadows deceive the eye. My bolts splinter harmlessly into tree trunks, wasting ammunition while the mercenaries track the muzzle flare and close the gap.

}
#if(v_perception == 3) {

I raise the repeating crossbow, letting my heightened vision lock onto their silhouettes.

Even in the deep darkness under the pines, every contour of their leather armor stands out sharply. Landing center-mass shots is as straightforward as target practice.

}
choice("Rely on speed and use melee attacks", Ch3-Speed, v_current_scene = Ch3-Speed) if (v_perception < 3)
choice("Try to aim the crossbow while moving", Ch3-Move-second, v_current_scene = Ch3-Move-second) if (v_perception < 3)
choice("Use fallen trees for throwing and clobbering", Ch3-Clobber, v_current_scene = Ch3-Clobber) if (v_ch3_lift_tree == 1 && v_perception < 3)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Snipe2, v_current_scene = Ch3-Snipe2) if (v_perception == 3)


ID: Ch3-Move-first
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_ch3_lift_tree == 0 && v_combat_technique < 3 || v_ch3_lift_tree == 1 && v_combat_technique < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_combat_technique == 3)
#if(v_combat_technique < 3) {

I keep my boots moving, weaving between trunks while firing the repeating crossbow on the run.

Running and shooting at night proves far harder than theory suggests. My bolts fly wild into the brush, while return fire inches closer with every stride.

}
#if(v_combat_technique == 3) {

I keep my boots moving, weaving between trunks while firing the repeating crossbow on the run.

Ten against one. Running blind invites a crossfire, but advanced combat technique turns the terrain into armor. I track the position of every hostile in the grove, calculating angles of approach to keep tree trunks between myself and their main firing lanes. By managing their collective blind spots, I ensure no more than two mercenaries can line up a shot at any given second.

}
choice("Rely on speed and use melee attacks", Ch3-Speed, v_current_scene = Ch3-Speed) if (v_combat_technique < 3)
choice("Snipe them from a distance", Ch3-Snipe-second, v_current_scene = Ch3-Snipe-second) if (v_combat_technique < 3)
