ID: Ch3-Clobber
TEXT:

I spot a fallen spruce trunk—four hundred pounds of seasoned timber.

I hoist the log over my shoulder, step out, and launch it two-handed through the brush. The massive trunk crashes through the patrol like a siege boulder, crushing five mercenaries into the dirt with a deafening splintering of bone and timber.

"Monster!" one shrieks in terror, firing his crossbow wildly.

I rip a second log from the ground, catching his bolt in the thick bark, and swing the trunk like a greatclub. The blow drives the mercenary's skull into an oak tree with concussive force, reducing bone and brain to red paste on the bark.

The remaining four mercenaries break into screams. One trips over his own boots, another soils his trousers in panic, and the last two sprint blindly into the darkness.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Clobber2, v_current_scene = Ch3-Clobber2)


ID: Ch3-Clobber2
TEXT:

#if(v_ch3_final_decision == 1 && v_ch3_prioritize < 4) {
I let the runners go. Broken deserters won't rally. I leave the wreckage behind and push deeper toward the command position.

}
#if(v_ch3_final_decision == 2 && v_ch3_prioritize < 4) {
I let the runners go. Broken deserters won't rally.

What follows is an absolute rout. Armed with four-hundred-pound logs, I tear through their firing lines with terrifying force. Half the battalion is crushed in minutes; the remainder scatter in terror through the night woods.

}
#if(v_ch3_final_decision == 1 && v_ch3_prioritize == 4) {
First, the runners. Running in a straight line through the trees makes them easy marks; I heave another log after them. The timber lands square across their spines, crushing both instantly.

Running out of manageable logs, I lift a jagged granite boulder and hurl it at the mercenary scrambling up from the mud. The rock strikes his chest with enough momentum to launch him backward into an oak trunk, caving his ribs.

The final man—the one who soiled himself—kneels in the dirt, weeping.

"Mercy! Please!"

"No," I say, picking up a heavy oak limb and crushing his skull.

}
#if(v_ch3_final_decision == 2 && v_ch3_prioritize == 4) {
First, the runners. Running in a straight line through the trees makes them easy marks; I heave another log after them. The timber lands square across their spines, crushing both instantly.

Running out of manageable logs, I lift a jagged granite boulder and hurl it at the mercenary scrambling up from the mud. The rock strikes his chest with enough momentum to launch him backward into an oak trunk, caving his ribs.

The final man—the one who soiled himself—kneels in the dirt, weeping.

"Mercy! Please!"

"No," I say, picking up a heavy oak limb and crushing his skull.

What follows is total annihilation. Armed with boulders and logs, I hunt down every fire team in the grove. None escape.

}
choice("Continue", Ch3-Crossbowmen-finish, v_current_scene = Ch3-Crossbowmen-finish) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 2 && v_ch3_prioritize == 4 || v_ch3_final_decision == 2 && v_ch3_prioritize < 4)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Leader-finish, v_current_scene = Ch3-Leader-finish) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 1 && v_ch3_prioritize == 4 && v_is_dead == 0 || v_ch3_final_decision == 1 && v_is_dead == 0 && v_ch3_prioritize < 4)


ID: Ch3-Snipe2
TEXT:

#if(v_ch3_prioritize < 3) {
I avoid lethal zones, aiming strictly for knees and thighs.

One by one, bolts find their marks from the deep shadows. The mercenaries scramble behind cover, trying to locate my muzzle flash, but my observation cuts through every gap in the foliage.

Whenever a man dashes between trunks, a bolt drops him. Whenever another tries to flank wide, I pin his leg from thirty yards out.

The last man standing drops his crossbow and flees in terror into the dark woods.

I let him run. His will is broken; he won't return.

}
#if(v_ch3_prioritize == 3) {
No quarter. I shoot to kill.

One by one, bolts pierce throats and chests from the deep shadows. The mercenaries scramble behind cover, trying to locate my muzzle flash, but my observation cuts through every gap in the foliage.

Whenever a man dashes between trunks, an iron tip drops him dead. Whenever another tries to flank wide, I punch a bolt through his sternum from thirty yards out.

The last man standing drops his crossbow and flees in terror into the dark woods.

I let him run. His will is broken; he won't return.

}
#if(v_ch3_prioritize == 4) {
No quarter. I shoot to kill.

One by one, bolts pierce throats and chests from the deep shadows. The mercenaries scramble behind cover, trying to locate my muzzle flash, but my observation cuts through every gap in the foliage.

Whenever a man dashes between trunks, an iron tip drops him dead. Whenever another tries to flank wide, I punch a bolt through his sternum from thirty yards out.

The last man breaks into a frantic sprint to escape the grove.

My vision locks onto his fleeing form. I lead the target and release—the bolt drives through the base of his skull, dropping him mid-stride.

}
choice("Continue", Ch3-Snipe-crossbowmen, v_current_scene = Ch3-Snipe-crossbowmen) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 2 && v_ch3_prioritize == 3 && v_is_dead == 0 || v_ch3_final_decision == 2 && v_ch3_prioritize == 4 && v_is_dead == 0 || v_ch3_final_decision == 2 && v_is_dead == 0 && v_ch3_prioritize < 3)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Leader-finish, v_current_scene = Ch3-Leader-finish) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 1 && v_ch3_prioritize == 3 && v_is_dead == 0 || v_ch3_final_decision == 1 && v_ch3_prioritize == 4 && v_is_dead == 0 || v_ch3_final_decision == 1 && v_is_dead == 0 && v_ch3_prioritize < 3)


ID: Ch3-Move2
TEXT:

#if(v_ch3_prioritize < 3) {
I aim for legs and hips, disabling without killing.

On the run, I count each mercenary's shots, timing my advances between their reload cycles. I prioritize targets actively aiming at my vector.

One down. Two down. The patrol panics under my unpredictable movement, their aim disintegrating as their line collapses.

The last man standing drops his weapon and bolts into the woods.

I let him go. He is finished fighting tonight.

}
#if(v_ch3_prioritize == 3) {
No holding back. I strike to kill.

On the run, I count each mercenary's shots, timing my advances between their reload cycles. I prioritize targets actively aiming at my vector, putting iron bolts through chests and throats.

One down. Two down. The patrol panics under my unpredictable movement, their aim disintegrating as their line collapses.

The last man standing drops his weapon and bolts into the woods.

I let him go. He is finished fighting tonight.

}
#if(v_ch3_prioritize == 4) {
No holding back. I strike to kill.

On the run, I count each mercenary's shots, timing my advances between their reload cycles. I prioritize targets actively aiming at my vector, putting iron bolts through chests and throats.

One down. Two down. The patrol panics under my unpredictable movement, their aim disintegrating as their line collapses.

The last man breaks into a desperate run for the pines.

I track his stride, leading the shot by half a pace. The bolt punches through the back of his neck, killing him on the spot.

}
choice("Continue", Ch3-Move-crossbowmen, v_current_scene = Ch3-Move-crossbowmen) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 2 && v_ch3_prioritize == 3 && v_is_dead == 0 || v_ch3_final_decision == 2 && v_ch3_prioritize == 4 && v_is_dead == 0 || v_ch3_final_decision == 2 && v_is_dead == 0 && v_ch3_prioritize < 3)
