ID: Ch3-Crossbowmen-finish
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch3_army,1)
achievement("One man army",v_ac_ch3_army)
The last man standing—their commander—drops to his knees in the bloodstained needles, weeping uncontrollably. His embroidered velvet tunic and gold-stitched mantle belong in a high court, not a dark forest. It explains how he bought an entire company of killers for a tournament bid.

"Mercy!" he wails in his shrill, reedy voice, hands trembling in the dirt. "I only entered for glory! I never meant to harm you! Spare me! I have wealth—take it all! Just let me live!"

He unclips a heavy velvet purse from his belt and hurls it at my boots. Gold coins spill across the moss. There is enough here to buy an estate in the Western Continent and live in luxury for the rest of my life.

choice("Take his money and spare his life", Ch3-Alone-Spare-Take, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Spare-Take, v_ch3_treasure = 1)
choice("Spare his life but don't take his money", Ch3-Alone-Spare-Leave, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Spare-Leave, v_ch3_treasure = 0)
choice("Kill him, and take his money", Ch3-Alone-Kill-Take, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Kill-Take, v_ch3_treasure = 1)
choice("Kill him, but don't take his money", Ch3-Alone-Kill-Leave, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Kill-Leave, v_ch3_treasure = 0)
choice("Pressure him into telling me where he's hiding the rest of his gold", Ch3-Alone-Pressure, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Pressure, v_ch3_treasure = 2)


ID: Ch3-Leader-finish
TEXT:

I cannot afford to trade shots with skirmishers all night. My objective is their commander.

I move silently through the outer brush, reading line-of-sight angles to slip past the patrols. I track the shrill shouting to a raised knoll fifty yards back. The commander stands behind a thin security detail of four personal guards, completely oblivious to his perimeter collapsing.

I stalk through the shadows, dropping the outer sentries with silent ice-dagger thrusts before stepping onto the knoll. Two rapid crossbow bolts drop the remaining bodyguards into the moss.

Their leader turns, freezing in place as he realizes he is alone. His silk doublet and gold-threaded mantle belong in a western palace, not a forest skirmish.

"What..." he stammers, backing away in terror. "Where are the guards? Guards!"

"Nobody is coming," I say, stepping out of the pines with the repeating crossbow leveled at his chest. "Your perimeter is gone. It's just you and me."

"Stay back! Don't touch me!"

I step forward, driving him against an oak trunk and twisting a fist into the collar of his tunic.

"Listen closely. I don't care what western estate you crawled out of, but you are my hostage now. Order every man in this forest to drop their weapons and surrender to the ice mage in the clearing, or I put a steel bolt through your throat and hunt down what's left of your guards."

"I... I can't!"

"You can. That horn on your belt doubles as an enchanted voice magnifier. Speak into it now, before my trigger finger twitches."

Trembling violently, he unclips the horn, brings it to his lips, and screams into the brass funnel:

"Attention, all ranks! This is the Duke of Bagelberry! I have been taken! Cease fire immediately! Step out of the timber, lay down your weapons, and surrender!"

The horn's amplified bellow rolls across the valley. The relentless hammering against Kate's frost dome abruptly dies. The forest falls dead silent.

"Did you not hear me?!" the duke shrieks into the horn. "As your lord, I COMMAND you to throw down your arms! Now!"

After a tense pause, the first mercenaries emerge from the shadows, tossing their repeating crossbows into the dirt. Dozens follow, forming a disarmed circle around Kate's glowing frost dome.

"There! I did it!" the duke sobs, his knees giving out. "Now let me go!"

"Why should I? As I recall, you promised us a quick throat-slit if we surrendered."

"No!" he screams, collapsing at my feet. "Please! I only wanted renown! I'll give you everything—take my gold, take all of it! Just spare my life!"

He hurls a heavy velvet purse onto the needles. Gold coins spill across the moss—enough to buy an estate and live in luxury for decades.

choice("Take his money and spare his life", Ch3-Alone-Spare-Take, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Spare-Take, v_ch3_treasure = 1)
choice("Spare his life but don't take his money", Ch3-Alone-Spare-Leave, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Spare-Leave, v_ch3_treasure = 0)
choice("Kill him, and take his money", Ch3-Alone-Kill-Take, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Kill-Take, v_ch3_treasure = 1)
choice("Kill him, but don't take his money", Ch3-Alone-Kill-Leave, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Kill-Leave, v_ch3_treasure = 0)
choice("Pressure him into telling me where he's hiding the rest of his gold", Ch3-Alone-Pressure, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Pressure, v_ch3_treasure = 2)


ID: Ch3-Alone-Spare-Take
TEXT:

Looking down at the groveling noble, I doubt he carries enough spine to ever enter these woods again.

"Take your life," I say, scooping up the pouch of gold. "Get out of my sight and don't look back."

"Bless you! You will never see me again!"

He scrambles to his feet and bolts blindly through the trees. I watch until the sound of his boots fades into the distance, then turn back toward Kate's position.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 2)


ID: Ch3-Alone-Spare-Leave
TEXT:

Looking down at the groveling noble, I doubt he carries enough spine to ever enter these woods again.

"Keep your gold," I say, kicking the pouch aside. "Get out of my sight and don't look back."

"Bless you! You will never see me again!"

He grabs his purse and bolts blindly through the trees. I watch until the sound of his boots fades into the distance, then turn back toward Kate's position.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 2)


ID: Ch3-Alone-Kill-Take
TEXT:

I raise the repeating crossbow and put a steel bolt through his skull before his next breath draws. In my position, he wouldn't have hesitated for a fraction of a second.

I pocket the purse of gold and walk back through the dark pines toward Kate.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 2)


ID: Ch3-Alone-Kill-Leave
TEXT:

I raise the repeating crossbow and put a steel bolt through his skull before his next breath draws. In my position, he wouldn't have hesitated for a fraction of a second.

I leave the heavy pouch of gold in the mud—useless ballast on the march.

I turn and walk back through the dark pines toward Kate.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 2)


ID: Ch3-Alone-Pressure
TEXT:

"You claim this is all your wealth," I say, tapping the crossbow against his breastbone. "A western duke doesn't travel without an emergency reserve. Where is the rest?"

"That is all I carried!" he stammers, clutching his collar. "The rest is in my western manor!"

"I know how warlords think. You wouldn't keep your entire purse in one satchel on an ambush. Where is the cache?"

"I swear by the gods, that is everything!"

"Unfortunate."

I level the iron sights directly between his eyes and slowly take up the slack on the trigger.

"Wait! The cedar!" he shrieks, flailing toward a thick pine behind us. "Under the flat granite slab! That is the last of it, I swear on my life!"

I walk to the marked tree and pry up the stone, unearthing an iron-bound strongbox packed with gold bullion and cut gems—three times the value of his belt pouch.

"You see?" the duke whimpers from the dirt. "It is all yours! Every coin!"

choice("Spare his life", Ch3-Alone-Pressure-Spare, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Pressure-Spare)
choice("Kill him anyway", Ch3-Alone-Pressure-Kill, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Pressure-Kill)


ID: Ch3-Alone-Pressure-Spare
TEXT:

"Take your life," I say, hoisting the heavy strongbox. "Get out of our sight and don't return."

"Yes! Bless you! Never again, I swear it!"

He scrambles to his feet and sprints blindly through the timber. I watch until his footsteps fade into the night, then carry the treasure back toward Kate.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 2)


ID: Ch3-Alone-Pressure-Kill
TEXT:

"Am... am I free to go?" the duke stammers from the dirt.

"You are free," I say, centering the iron sights on his forehead. "Forever."

The bowstring snaps. The bolt punches clean through his skull, dropping him instantly into the pine needles.

I gather the strongbox and the velvet purse, turning back toward Kate's position.

choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 1)
choice("Continue", Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return, v_current_scene = Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return) if (v_ch3_final_decision == 2)


ID: Ch3-Alone-Leader-Return
TEXT:

#if(v_ch2_kate_debt == 0 && v_ch3_prioritize < 4) {
I step into the clearing and stop cold.

Every mercenary who emerged from the tree line to surrender lies sprawled across the moss, impaled on jagged spikes of ice. Blood steams in the cold air.

"Kate," I breathe, staring at the slaughter. "What did you do?"

"I granted them a swift death," she says coldly, wiping frost from her sleeves. "Isn't that what they promised us?"

"They surrendered. They threw down their weapons."

"And what did you expect us to do with them?" she snaps, turning to face me. "March a hundred prisoners through a warzone? Tie them to trees to starve or be butchered by the next mage who walks by? If we let them walk, they would have regrouped under a new officer and ambushed us tomorrow. There was no other outcome."

I look at the bloodstained needles, the harsh reality settling in.

"I... suppose you're right. Let's get back to the cave."

"I'll be honest," Kate says as we take the trail back. "I didn't expect you to pull that off."

"Neither did I."

"That makes two debts I owe you, Barry. Have you considered opening a bank?"

"I'll look into a charter after the tournament."

We hike the rest of the mountain path in silence. After a dawn spent in blood, the quiet is welcome.

}
