ID: Ch3-Alone-Crossbowmen-Return
TEXT:

#if(v_ch2_kate_debt == 0 && v_ch3_bloodied == 0) {
As I step into the clearing, Kate lowers her frost shields.

"Barry? Why did the firing stop?"

"Because I eliminated them."

Kate stares at me, letting the words sink in.

"You took out the entire battalion?"

"Every one of them. They won't bother us again. Let's get back to camp."

"I'll be honest," Kate says as we take the mountain trail back. "I didn't expect you to pull that off."

"Neither did I."

"That makes two debts I owe you, Barry. Have you considered opening a bank?"

"I'll look into a charter after the tournament."

We hike the rest of the trail in silence. After a dawn spent in blood, the quiet is welcome.

}
